{"name":"Goku Orange","hex":"#f0833a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"orange","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An evergreen tree of the genus Citrus such as Citrus sinensis which yields oranges (the fruit).","Any round citrus fruit with a yellow-red colour when ripe and a sour-sweet taste; the fruit of the orange tree.\n Specifically, a sweet orange or Citrus sinensis."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having the colour of the fruit of an orange tree; yellowred; reddish-yellow."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/orange"}],"entries":[{"title":"Goku","blocks":[{"text":"Son Goku is a fictional character and the main protagonist of the Dragon Ball manga series created by Akira Toriyama. He is based on Sun Wukong, a main character of the classic 16th-century Chinese novel Journey to the West, combined with influences from the Hong Kong action cinema of Jackie Chan and Bruce Lee. Goku made his debut in the first Dragon Ball chapter, Bulma and Son Goku, originally published in Japan's Weekly Shōnen Jump magazine on December 3, 1984."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/4c/GokumangaToriyama.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Goku","wikidata":"Q2142"},{"title":"Orange (colour)","blocks":[{"text":"Orange is the colour between yellow and red on the spectrum of visible light. The human eyes perceive orange when observing light with a dominant wavelength between roughly 585 and 620 nanometres. In traditional colour theory, it is a secondary colour of pigments, produced by mixing yellow and red. In the RGB colour model, it is a tertiary colour. It is named after the fruit of the same name."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Delicatearch.png/330px-Delicatearch.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orange_(colour)","wi